  program, but if you want to add a new license to a program, you can
  choose a different license instead of a license for network server
  software if you wish.

  The GNU Affero General Public License does not require you to publish your
  source code if you run the program on a server and make it available over
  the network, but you must make the source code available to users who are
  interacting with it remotely.

